@page "/layout-patterns/header-footer"
@layout HeaderFooterLayout

<PageTitle>HeaderFooterLayout pattern · UI Playbook</PageTitle>

<SectionContent SectionId="@HeaderFooterLayout.HeaderSection">
    <a class="layout-pattern-brand" href="components/header-footer-layout">Header / body contract</a>
</SectionContent>

<section class="layout-contract-page" aria-labelledby="header-footer-pattern-title" data-testid="header-footer-layout-pattern">
    <div class="layout-contract-page__intro">
        <span>Router-level layout pattern</span>
        <h1 id="header-footer-pattern-title">Header and main content layout</h1>
        <p>HeaderFooterLayout supplies the sticky header, user controls, section outlet, and body landmark. The page supplies the body content.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="layout-contract-page__grid">
        <article><strong>Header outlet</strong><p>Applications provide product identity and route-specific header content.</p></article>
        <article><strong>User controls</strong><p>Authentication and preferences remain composed by the shared header control.</p></article>
        <article><strong>Body main</strong><p>The layout owns the one main landmark and places the routed body inside it.</p></article>
    </div>
    <a class="layout-contract-page__back" href="components/header-footer-layout">Return to HeaderFooterLayout documentation</a>
</section>
